---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Transition to School Support | Marietta Childcare"
  description="Learn how Marietta Childcare prepares children for kindergarten with transition support and readiness activities.">
  <section class="relative py-32 overflow-hidden w-screen -ml-[calc((100vw-100%)/2)]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <img 
        src="/images/Background_Images/girl_reading_book_quiet_corner_background.jpg" 
        alt="School transition" 
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black mb-6 text-white drop-shadow-lg">Transition to School Support</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-12 max-w-2xl text-white drop-shadow-md">Kindergarten readiness preparation and transition support to help children succeed in school.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 px-6 lg:px-20">
    <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto">
      <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Transition to School Support at Marietta Childcare</h1>
        
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">Marietta Childcare provides comprehensive transition support for children moving to kindergarten. Marietta Childcare's transition program builds children's confidence and readiness for school.</p>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Kindergarten Readiness Assessment</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare assesses children's kindergarten readiness. Readiness assessment at Marietta Childcare evaluates academic, social, and emotional skills. Marietta Childcare's assessment identifies areas of strength and areas needing support.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare shares readiness assessment results with families. Assessment information at Marietta Childcare helps families understand their child's readiness. Marietta Childcare's assessment approach supports individualized transition planning.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Pre-Kindergarten Preparation</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare provides pre-kindergarten preparation activities. Preparation at Marietta Childcare includes academic skill building and classroom routine practice. Marietta Childcare's pre-kindergarten focus ensures children are ready for school demands.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare's preparation includes letter and number recognition, phonemic awareness, and early writing. Preparation activities at Marietta Childcare simulate kindergarten classroom experiences. Marietta Childcare's pre-kindergarten approach builds children's confidence.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">School Visits and Orientation</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare facilitates kindergarten school visits. School visits at Marietta Childcare help children become familiar with their new school. Marietta Childcare's visits include classroom tours and meeting teachers.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare organizes kindergarten orientation activities. Orientation at Marietta Childcare prepares children for the school environment. Marietta Childcare's visits reduce transition anxiety and build excitement.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Social-Emotional Preparation</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare emphasizes social-emotional skills for school transition. Social-emotional preparation at Marietta Childcare includes independence and self-regulation. Marietta Childcare teaches children to manage emotions and follow classroom rules.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare's social-emotional focus supports children's school adjustment. Preparation at Marietta Childcare includes practice with classroom expectations. Marietta Childcare's approach builds children's confidence for school success.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Parent Resources and Guidance</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare provides families with kindergarten transition resources. Resources at Marietta Childcare include information about school expectations and preparation. Marietta Childcare offers guidance on supporting children's transition at home.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare's resources help families prepare for kindergarten. Guidance at Marietta Childcare includes tips for managing transition anxiety. Marietta Childcare's parent support extends beyond childcare to family preparation.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Communication with Schools</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare communicates with kindergarten programs about children's development. School communication at Marietta Childcare includes sharing information about children's strengths and needs. Marietta Childcare's partnerships with schools support smooth transitions.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare provides transition information to kindergarten teachers. Information sharing at Marietta Childcare ensures continuity of care and education. Marietta Childcare's collaborative approach supports children's school success.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Confidence Building Activities</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare includes confidence-building activities for transition. Confidence activities at Marietta Childcare celebrate children's accomplishments and growth. Marietta Childcare's activities build children's self-esteem for school entry.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare's confidence-building approach reduces transition anxiety. Activities at Marietta Childcare help children feel prepared and excited. Marietta Childcare's support builds children's positive school attitudes.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Ongoing Support and Follow-Up</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare provides ongoing support after children transition to school. Follow-up at Marietta Childcare includes checking in with families about school adjustment. Marietta Childcare's support extends beyond the transition period.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare maintains relationships with families after school entry. Support at Marietta Childcare includes resources for school success. Marietta Childcare's commitment to children continues through kindergarten transition.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-blue-50 p-6 rounded-lg mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Prepare for Kindergarten Success</h3>
          <p class="mb-4">Marietta Childcare is committed to supporting children's transition to school. Contact Marietta Childcare to learn about transition support and kindergarten preparation.</p>
          <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-700 transition">Contact Us</a>
        </section>

        <nav class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related Pages</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li><a href="/faq/transition-to-kindergarten" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">How Do You Prepare for Kindergarten?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/faq/curriculum" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">What's Your Curriculum?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/programs" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Our Programs</a></li>
            <li><a href="/faq/parent-communication" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">How Do You Communicate with Parents?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Contact Marietta Childcare</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
